WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.194 --> 00:00:04.782
We're in Penajóia, in Almada.
It's a recent, self-built neighbourhood,

2
00:00:04.866 --> 00:00:08.549
whose main feature
is that it grew very quickly.

3
00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:12.831
It began with a few houses, and today,
from here, there are over a thousand,

4
00:00:12.915 --> 00:00:14.585
I don't know exactly how many.

5
00:00:15.095 --> 00:00:19.927
The extraordinary thing about
this neighbourhood is that the land it

6
00:00:20.011 --> 00:00:23.888
stands on doesn't belong
to the people: it's State land.

7
00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:26.535
The housing institute,
IHRU, owns most of it, not all.

8
00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:28.710
And faced with this, I wonder.

9
00:00:28.938 --> 00:00:31.113
I sat in the Constituent
Assembly 50 years ago,

10
00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:35.831
we passed the Constitution and we
passed Article 65, the right to housing,

11
00:00:35.915 --> 00:00:39.161
a right that hadn't been
in the Constitution, and then it was.

12
00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:41.923
And one of the things that right,
that article, says

13
00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:45.506
is that it's up to the State
to do a number of things.

14
00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.843
And one of the things
that falls to the Portuguese State,

15
00:00:49.094 --> 00:00:56.370
under Article 65 of the Constitution,
is to support people's own initiatives

16
00:00:56.454 --> 00:01:00.580
to solve their housing problems,
and to support self-building.

17
00:01:00.664 --> 00:01:05.558
Here's a case that could and should have
been supported from day one. It wasn't,

18
00:01:05.769 --> 00:01:07.580
and it still isn't.

19
00:01:07.664 --> 00:01:10.991
I think this is serious,
because this is just one example,

20
00:01:11.075 --> 00:01:14.639
and there must be many more in Portugal,
self-built neighbourhoods

21
00:01:14.723 --> 00:01:16.273
that people built

22
00:01:16.357 --> 00:01:20.115
on land that isn't theirs,
because no one gave them any opportunity.

23
00:01:20.199 --> 00:01:23.102
They can't live on the street,
and they don't want to,

24
00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:27.778
they want to give their children a roof,
and they want neighbours, and family,

25
00:01:27.862 --> 00:01:31.259
and what anyone would naturally
want from the right to housing.

26
00:01:31.343 --> 00:01:33.646
Not just a home for one,
but for them and their family.

27
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:37.763
So I came here, I'd been here before,

28
00:01:37.894 --> 00:01:42.668
but to stress the urgency
of drawing attention to this.

29
00:01:42.752 --> 00:01:46.051
We have a Constitution in force,
binding on everyone,

30
00:01:46.135 --> 00:01:48.159
giving rights to citizens,
duties to the State,

31
00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:51.222
and duties to citizens too,
some, naturally,

32
00:01:51.306 --> 00:01:55.140
and this right to housing
can't go on being ignored.
